  "purpose": "True-scale visual lock for Gary Eats. Another model should flag any asset whose style or camera does not match Gary and the shops.",
  "camera": "Not a vanishing-point street. Lanes are flat bands. Shops are front-on with a little of the top showing. Props use that same camera. Gary is from behind, head turned so the face is visible. One ground line. One light, soft daylight, from the left.",
  "style": "Painted British cartoon. Clean dark outlines. Semi-realistic, not cute, not pixel, not photo. Gary is the most realistic asset. Shops are flatter painted sets. Props, food and hazards sit between them, closer to the shop than to Gary.",
  "scale_rule": "Gary is the ruler at 142 canvas px tall. A plate is about a third of his height. A hazard is no taller than a plate. A bin, postbox, bench or board is between his knee and his chest. A tree is about chest height. A shop is taller than him.",
  "sheet": "ASSET_GRID.png. 1 game canvas pixel = 2 sheet pixels. Background is the game canvas colour #1a1e24.",
